meta {
  name: Key Policy - Get
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/:workspace/ai-key-policy
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  workspace: {{workspaceId}}
}

docs {
  The workspace's rules for its own AI provider keys. Requires
  `ai-credential.view` — anyone who can see the keys can see why a model
  is unavailable or their personal key isn't used.

  - `platform_usage` — `fallback` (own key first, platform key as
    backup), `when_no_key` (platform key only for models no own key
    covers) or `never`.
  - `allow_personal_keys` — whether members may add personal keys.
  - `can_manage` — whether the caller may change it.

  Response is wrapped:
  `{ success, statusCode, message, data: { policy: { platform_usage, allow_personal_keys, can_manage, updated_at } } }`.
}
